Upstream-bound: no
Subject: [PORT_HOST] P6.4 turbo: menus report that they are waiting (menus run at 1.5x)

P6.4 / owner decision 2026-10-27 ("pode acelerar os menus um pouco, algo tipo
50%"). `updateFieldMenu` (`engine/menu/field_menu.c`) calls
`dw3_port_turbo_menu_frame()` (port/options/turbo.c) at the top of each update.
The turbo policy stamps the frame; while the stamp is current and the mode is
the field, fast-forward runs at 1.5x instead of the full setting. The task
hosts the field menu list, the port Options / Cheats screen (patch 0160) and
the Return to title Yes / No window (patch 0123), so one call covers them. A
killed task stops stamping, so nothing can stay stuck at the slow speed.

Battle: `FIGHTSTG_updateCursor` (`battle/battle_mode/cursor.c`) makes the same
call while its cursor is not locked, that is, while a menu waits for the player
(the command menu, the technique, item, switch and digivolve lists all use it).
The Yes / No and Options paths of the battle are not involved (Options over a
held battle stays at 1x). No game state is read or changed.

